# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is ignored by Git. Never commit real values.
# Every setting can also be supplied as a real environment variable.
#
# The server reads a settings file only when told which one, so a file left in the
# folder it happens to start in cannot change its settings:
#   export DATAVERSE_ENV_FILE=/full/path/to/.env

# --- Required: where and how to sign in -------------------------------------
# Address of the Dataverse environment: https and host only, no path.
DATAVERSE_URL=https://your-environment.example.com
# Microsoft Entra tenant ID (GUID) or tenant domain.
DATAVERSE_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# Application (client) ID of the app registration.
DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Set exactly one credential. A certificate is preferred over a secret.
DATAVERSE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# DATAVERSE_CLIENT_CERTIFICATE_PATH=/path/to/private-key.pem
# DATAVERSE_CLIENT_CERTIFICATE_THUMBPRINT=

# --- Optional: Microsoft cloud ----------------------------------------------
# Sign-in address. Commercial and GCC use the default.
# GCC High and DoD use https://login.microsoftonline.us
# DATAVERSE_AUTHORITY_HOST=https://login.microsoftonline.com
# DATAVERSE_API_VERSION=v9.2

# --- Optional: logging -------------------------------------------------------
# DATAVERSE_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# --- What the agent may use --------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated IDs of the system views the data owner has approved.
# Only these views can be listed, described, counted, or read.
DATAVERSE_APPROVED_VIEW_IDS=
# For local testing only: make every active system view available. Leave false otherwise.
# DATAVERSE_ALLOW_ALL_SYSTEM_VIEWS=false
# How long view definitions are cached, in seconds. 0 turns caching off.
# DATAVERSE_VIEW_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=60
# Comma-separated logical names of tables find_record may search by name
# (for example, the office table). Empty means find_record is off.
DATAVERSE_SEARCHABLE_TABLES=
# Most matches find_record returns (1 to 50).
# DATAVERSE_FIND_RECORD_LIMIT=10
# A view's displayed columns can be filtered. List extra columns here to allow them too,
# as table.column, comma-separated (for example the office column, if views do not
# display it). Leave empty unless the data owner agrees.
# DATAVERSE_EXTRA_FILTER_COLUMNS=

# --- Limits -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Most rows run_view returns per page (1 to 250). Keep it small.
# DATAVERSE_MAX_PAGE_SIZE=50
# DATAVERSE_HTTP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
# How many times to retry when Dataverse throttles or is unreachable (0 to 6).
# DATAVERSE_MAX_RETRIES=3
# Longest single wait Dataverse may ask for before the server gives up, in seconds.
# DATAVERSE_MAX_RETRY_WAIT_SECONDS=30

# --- Audit log ----------------------------------------------------------------
# One JSON line per tool call. Written to stderr unless a file is set here.
# The file is created readable only by its owner. Protect and retain it per your policy.
# DATAVERSE_AUDIT_LOG_PATH=/var/log/dataverse-views-mcp/audit.log
# Set to false to log a fingerprint in place of filter values and search text.
# DATAVERSE_AUDIT_LOG_VALUES=true
